.TH "SVGANIMATEDENUMERATION.ANIMVAL" "3JS" "July 9, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SVGAnimatedEnumeration.animVal \- SVGAnimatedEnumeration: animVal
property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]animVal\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]SVGAnimatedEnumeration\f[R] interface represents the value of an
SVG enumeration.
.PP
In SVG 2, \f[CR]animVal\f[R] reflects the non\-animated value of the
attribute: it is the same as \f[CR]baseVal\f[R] .
.SH VALUE
An integer representing the value of the enumeration.
.PP
The allowed values depend on the attribute that is reflected.
This property cannot be written.
.SH EXCEPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]NoModificationAllowedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the property is set to any value.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]div\f[R]>
  <\f[B]svg\f[R] viewBox=\(dq0 0 100 100\(dq width=\(dq200\(dq height=\(dq200\(dq>
    <\f[B]clipPath\f[R] id=\(dqclip1\(dq clipPathUnits=\(dquserSpaceOnUse\(dq>
      <\f[B]animate\f[R]
        attributeName=\(dqclipPathUnits\(dq
        values=\(dquserSpaceOnUse;objectBoundingBox;userSpaceOnUse\(dq
        dur=\(dq2s\(dq
        repeatCount=\(dqindefinite\(dq />
      <\f[B]circle\f[R] cx=\(dq50\(dq cy=\(dq50\(dq r=\(dq25\(dq />
    </\f[B]clipPath\f[R]>

    <\f[B]rect\f[R] id=\(dqr1\(dq x=\(dq0\(dq y=\(dq0\(dq width=\(dq50\(dq height=\(dq100\(dq />

    <\f[B]use\f[R] clip\-path=\(dqurl(#clip1)\(dq href=\(dq#r1\(dq fill=\(dqlightblue\(dq />
  </\f[B]svg\f[R]>
</\f[B]div\f[R]>
<\f[B]pre\f[R] id=\(dqlog\(dq></\f[B]pre\f[R]>
.EE
.PP
The following JavaScript gets the element, and logs the
\f[CR]animValue\f[R] of the \f[CR]SVGClipPathElement.clipPathUnits\f[R]
property.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] clipPath1 = document.getElementById(\(dqclip1\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] log = document.getElementById(\(dqlog\(dq);

\f[B]function\f[R] displayLog() {
  \f[B]const\f[R] animValue = clipPath1.clipPathUnits.animVal;
  \f[B]const\f[R] baseValue = clipPath1.clipPathUnits.baseVal;
  log.textContent = \(gaThe \(aqclipPathUnits.animVal\(aq is ${animValue}.\(rsn\(ga;
  requestAnimationFrame(displayLog);
}

displayLog();
.EE
